      "effect_p95": -1.9045631893497887,
      "effect_sd": 0.7752280914356747,
      "epochs": 100,
      "n": 20,
      "note": "Non-binding because the whole null distribution is negative, so it imposes no positive threshold and the structural floor governs.  LIMITATION: trained on a stream whose composition targets are permuted, the candidate is confidently wrong (4-6 nats against uniform log(10)=2.303), so the null is centred far below zero.  It therefore bounds the false-positive tail of the decision statistic but does NOT calibrate its variance in a near-competitive regime.",
